1. Create a new plugin directory in the WordPress plugins folder.
2. Create a PHP file for the plugin and include the necessary header comments.
3. Register a custom post type for the posts that will be created.
4. Create a shortcode for the form that will be used to input the text and settings.
5. Process the form data and split the text into chunks based on the specified word count.
6. Create a new post for each chunk of text and add the relevant headers and details.
7. Save the posts and return a success message.

Here's an example implementation of the plugin:

1. Create a new directory in the WordPress plugins folder called `text-splitter`.
2. Create a new file in the `text-splitter` directory called `text-splitter.php`.
3. Add the following header comments to the `text-splitter.php` file:
```php
<?php
/**
 * Plugin Name: Text Splitter
 * Plugin URI: https://example.com/text-splitter
 * Description: A plugin to split large amounts of text into smaller chunks and create posts for each chunk.
 * Version: 1.0.0
 * Author: Your Name
 * Author URI: https://example.com
 * License: GPL2
 */
```
4. Register a custom post type for the posts that will be created:
```php
function text_splitter_register_post_type() {
    $args = array(
        'public' => true,
        'label'  => 'Text Splitter',
        'supports' => array( 'title', 'editor' ),
    );
    register_post_type( 'text_splitter', $args );
}
add_action( 'init', 'text_splitter_register_post_type' );
```
5. Create a shortcode for the form:
```php
function text_splitter_shortcode() {
    ob_start();
    ?>
    <form method="post" action="">
        <label for="word_count">Word Count:</label>
        <input type="number" name="word_count" id="word_count" required>
        <br>
        <label for="title">Title:</label>
        <input type="text" name="title" id="title" required>
        <br>
        <label for="body">Body:</label>
        <textarea name="body" id="body" rows="10" cols="50" required></textarea>
        <br>
        <input type="submit" name="submit" value="Process">
    </form>
    <?php
    return ob_get_clean();
}
add_shortcode( 'text_splitter', 'text_splitter_shortcode' );
```
6. Process the form data and split the text into chunks:
```php
function text_splitter_process_form() {
    if ( isset( $_POST['submit'] ) ) {
        $word_count = intval( $_POST['word_count'] );
        $title = sanitize_text_field( $_POST['title'] );
        $body = sanitize_textarea_field( $_POST['body'] );

        $words = explode( ' ', $body );
        $chunks = array_chunk( $words, $word_count );

        $post_count = 1;
        foreach ( $chunks as $chunk ) {
            $post_title = sprintf( '%s %03d', $title, $post_count );
            $post_content = implode( ' ', $chunk );

            $post_id = wp_insert_post( array(
                'post_title' => $post_title,
                'post_content' => $post_content,
                'post_type' => 'text_splitter',
                'post_status' => 'publish',
            ) );

            $post_count++;
        }

        wp_redirect( add_query_arg( 'message', 'success', $_SERVER['REQUEST_URI'] ) );
        exit;
    }
}
add_action( 'template_redirect', 'text_splitter_process_form' );
```
7. Display a success message after the form is processed:
```php
function text_splitter_success_message() {
    if ( isset( $_GET['message'] ) && 'success' === $_GET['message'] ) {
        echo '<div class="notice notice-success is-dismissible"><p>The text has been split into posts.</p></div>';
    }
}
add_action( 'admin_notices', 'text_splitter_success_message' );
```
To use the plugin, activate it in the WordPress admin area and add the `[text_splitter]` shortcode to a page or post. The form will be displayed and the text can be input and processed. The resulting posts will be created with the specified headers and details.
